secubox-hardening (1.0.2-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fix navbar visibility (closes #389):
    - The 1.0.1 attempt didn't actually take effect on installed
      boards because debian/rules installed the menu from
      debian/menu.json (category: "security", which is NOT one of
      the 6 charter categories — hub silently dropped it). The
      menu.d/ source file was orphaned and never read by the build.
    - Delete the stray packages/secubox-hardening/debian/menu.json.
    - debian/rules: replace the bespoke
      `install -m 644 debian/menu.json …/120-hardening.json` with
      the standard `[ -d menu.d ] && cp -r menu.d/.` pattern that
      every other package uses.
  * After this, the package actually ships
    menu.d/105-hardening.json with category=root, order=105
    (between Admin@100 and Rezapp@494 in the root menu).

