secubox-hardening (1.0.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=low

  * Move menu entry from category "wall" → "root" (closes #389).
    Hardening is proactive system-level config (sysctl, AppArmor,
    kernel modules), not a threat-response enforcer like the wall
    siblings (CrowdSec, WAF, threats). Natural neighbour to
    secubox-admin / secubox-system / secubox-vault in root.
    NOTE: this changelog entry shipped but the rules bug above
    prevented the new menu file from actually being installed —
    fixed in 1.0.2.
  * Rename menu file 120-hardening.json → 105-hardening.json to
    reflect the new order between Admin@100 and Rezapp@494.
  * Description widened to enumerate the hardening scope.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Wed, 27 May 2026 18:00:00 +0000

